This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**
   - **"i can't login for emrekabakci@gmail.com on prod"** — diagnose a production login failure.
   - Via AskUserQuestion the user clarified the symptom: **"Bounced back to the login page"** on **"Google, Magic link (email), all of them including slack"**.
   - **"cant you use my lobu browser"** — a correction: use the paired **Owletto extension via the Lobu connector-operations bridge** (`client.operations.execute`), not `claude-in-chrome` (whose extension was not connected).
   - **"so tell me what's the proper fix here"** — the user wanted the real root-cause fix, not a workaround (consistent with their standing rule: "Prefer the proper fix (add the missing capability) over routing around the gap").
   - **"fix it properly same pr"** — implement all fix layers in a single PR.
   - **"do that"** — interpreted as: proceed with merging PR #2558 and carrying through to prod verification. Deliberately NOT interpreted as authorization to delete the stray org/account (destructive, ambiguous).

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - **RFC 6265 §5.4 cookie ordering**: equal-path cookies are sent **oldest-first**; server resolves the **first** occurrence. A stale host-only cookie therefore permanently outranks every newer domain-scoped one → unrecoverable login brick.
   - **Cookie scope twins**: host-only (`app.lobu.ai`) vs domain-scoped (`Domain=.lobu.ai`) cookies of the same name coexist.
   - **better-auth 1.6.8** cookie signing: `\`${token}.${makeSignature(token, secret)}\``, where `makeSignature` uses `btoa(...)` = **standard base64 (padded)**, NOT base64url. Cookie name gets `__Secure-` prefix when secure.
   - `useSecureCookies` is keyed on `NODE_ENV === "production" || https configured origin` (`auth/index.tsx:893`) — **not** on the request's forwarded proto.
   - Browsers **reject** any `Set-Cookie` for a `__Secure-`-prefixed name lacking `Secure`; and JS cannot overwrite/delete an HttpOnly cookie.
   - `__Host-` prefix would prevent duplicates structurally but forbids `Domain` — not viable given `{org}.lobu.ai` session sharing.
   - Prod infra: CNPG cluster `lobu-ai-prod-db`, ns `summaries-prod`, DB named `owletto`, `-c postgres` required; SealedSecret `summaries-app-secrets` injected via `envFrom` (so pods keep their start-time env).
   - Owletto bridge ops: `navigate`, `evaluate`, `close_tab`, `network_intercept_start/drain/stop`, `get_accessibility_tree`, `screenshot`.

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   - **`packages/server/src/auth/session-cookie-scope.ts` (NEW, ~139 lines)** — the core primitives. Exports `SESSION_COOKIE_BASENAME`, `sessionCookieName(isHttps)`, `countNamedCookies(header, name)`, `hostOnlyExpiry(name, secure)`, `convergeSetCookieScope(setCookies, opts)`, `convergeResponseCookieScope(response, opts)`.
     ```ts
     export const SESSION_COOKIE_BASENAME = "better-auth.session_token";

     export function hostOnlyExpiry(name: string, secure: boolean): string {
       const parts = [`${name}=`, "Path=/", "Max-Age=0", "HttpOnly", "SameSite=Lax"];
       if (secure) parts.push("Secure");
       return parts.join("; ");
     }

     export function convergeSetCookieScope(
       setCookies: string[],
       opts: { cookieDomain?: string; isHttps: boolean },
     ): string[] {
       if (!opts.cookieDomain) return setCookies;
       const out = [...setCookies];
       const expired = new Set<string>();
       for (const setCookie of setCookies) {
         const eq = setCookie.indexOf("=");
         if (eq === -1) continue;
         const name = setCookie.slice(0, eq).trim();
         if (!name || expired.has(name)) continue;
         if (!/;\s*Domain=/i.test(setCookie)) continue;
         if (isExpiry(setCookie)) continue;
         expired.add(name);
         // Mirror the source cookie's Secure, not just our own https detection
         const secure = opts.isHttps || /;\s*Secure\s*(;|$)/i.test(setCookie);
         out.push(hostOnlyExpiry(name, secure));
       }
       return out;
     }
     ```

   - **`packages/server/src/index.ts`** — the `/api/auth/*` chokepoint (covers every sign-in method at once, plus `state`/`pkce_code_verifier`). Added imports `resolveBaseUrl` from `./auth/base-url` and `convergeResponseCookieScope` from `./auth/session-cookie-scope`; changed `return auth.handler(request);` to:
     ```ts
     const response = await auth.handler(request);
     return convergeResponseCookieScope(response, {
       cookieDomain: process.env.AUTH_COOKIE_DOMAIN,
       isHttps: resolveBaseUrl({ request: c.req.raw }).startsWith("https://"),
     });
     ```

   - **`packages/server/src/auth/routes.ts`** — `mintSessionCookieValue` was the **production source** of the twin (set host-only). Now pushes `Domain=${cookieDomain}` and returns `hostOnlyExpiryHeader`; both call sites (`/exchange-token` at ~430, `/local-init` at ~753) append it with `{ append: true }`. Return type widened to include `hostOnlyExpiryHeader: string | null`.

   - **`packages/server/src/workspace/multi-tenant.ts`** — added duplicate-cookie `logger.warn` next to the existing first-match regex `/(?:__Secure-)?better-auth\.session_token=([^;]+)/` (~line 530).

   - **`packages/server/src/__tests__/unit/session-cookie-scope.test.ts` (NEW, bun:test, 9 tests)** — DB-free; this dir is what `make test-unit` runs and is excluded from vitest.

   - **`packages/server/src/auth/__tests__/exchange-token-cookie.test.ts`** — added wiring test `'GET /exchange-token scopes the cookie to the zone and expires the host-only twin'` asserting `Domain=.lobu.ai` on the setter and NO `Domain` on the expiry.

   - **`docs/BROWSER_TESTING.md`** — planted-cookie teardown made a mandatory step 5, plus a "### Always expire the planted cookie" section explaining the RFC ordering trap.

4. **Errors and fixes:**
   - **base64url vs base64 signing**: first cookie-signing attempt used base64url → `null`. Read better-auth source (`makeSignature` uses `btoa`) → standard padded base64 → full session returned.
   - **MAJOR wrong conclusion — "BETTER_AUTH_SECRET rotates on every deploy"**: I declared "**Found it.**" This was false. Prod rolled pods mid-session; `kubectl exec ... printenv BETTER_AUTH_SECRET 2>/dev/null` hit a dead pod, returned **empty**, and `HMAC("", token)` produced a plausible signature. Proved it: `HMAC("", "REDACTED") = REDACTED` — exactly my "old" sig. Corrected plainly to the user. Saved as `feedback_kubectl_printenv_can_silently_return_empty.md`. Fix pattern: length-assert every captured secret, never suppress stderr on the read.
   - **Invalid duplicate-precedence conclusion**: an earlier test claiming "duplicates fail in either order" used the same empty-secret cookie. Re-ran with a valid secret → **first-wins** (`dead; good` → null, `good; dead` → session).
   - **`make pre-pr` false green**: background wrapper reported exit 0 while `PRE_PR_EXIT=2` (5 TS2339/TS2353 errors from an un-widened return type on `mintSessionCookieValue`). Fixed the annotation; the explicit `echo $?` is what caught it.
   - **`make review-fix` quota**: default `auto` → codex, "You've hit your usage limit… try again at Aug 10th", exit 2, no edits. Re-ran `REVIEWER_CLI=claude CLAUDE_REVIEW_MODEL=fable` **in the foreground** (per memory: claude reviewer dies as a background task).
   - **Real latent bug found by the Fable fixer**: expiry derived `Secure` from `resolveBaseUrl`'s `isHttps`, which can diverge from better-auth's `useSecureCookies` (`NODE_ENV`-keyed). A `Secure`-less expiry for a `__Secure-` name is silently rejected → convergence no-ops. Now mirrors the source cookie's `Secure`; 9th test added.
   - **Apparent "reverts merged work"**: two-dot `git diff --stat origin/main` showed agent-worker deletions. Verified benign — `origin/main` had advanced by `c8b90563c` (#2556). Three-dot `origin/main...HEAD` is the mandated check and listed exactly the 7 intended files.
